## TD half

- New emissions where a genuine in-engine condition exists:
  * `Canceled` in cancel_production (AUDIO.CPP VOX_CANCELED, player-owned only)
  * `ReinforcementsArrived` in Action::CreateTeam (TACTION_CREATE_TEAM script)
- `td_eva_table_coverage` pins the reachable set: 13 distinct lines driven through
  real conditions (UnitReady, UnitLost, EnemyUnitDestroyed, StructureLost,
  EnemyStructureDestroyed, LowPower, BaseUnderAttack, InsufficientFunds,
  Canceled, ReinforcementsArrived, IonCannonReady, MissionAccomplished,
  MissionFailed).
- Honest scope note: the plan's ">=20 of 45" assumed ~29 more conditions exist;
  the engine tracks 16 distinct emitters (13 pinned + ConstructionComplete +
  UnableToBuildMore reached by other tests). The plan's own rule - never emit a
  line without an in-engine condition - forbids inventing the remaining table
  rows (TransportSighted, NeedHarvester, SilosNeeded, Repairing, ...), so they
  stay documented-only. ConstructionComplete's emitter exists
  (update_production building branch) but no suite scenario yet drives a queued
  building to completion in a quiet game (placement gating); documented, not faked.

